# Expected classification of tests/corpus/synthetic_small.log (one row per stream line).
# Columns: seq <TAB> primary <TAB> labels (comma-separated, alphabetical; '-' = none).
# Derived by hand from the "#@ rules:" annotations in the corpus and spec 5.3
# (highest severity wins, ties SEC > PII > AUTH > ERR > PERF; SSH_ACCEPTED gives no label).
#
# STATE: aggregator v0 (T1.7) - no validators, context keywords or correlator yet.
#   Consequences, to be revisited in T3.4/T5.1:
#   - seq 111 (bad Luhn), 117 and 119 (bad Verhoeff), 168 (14-digit timestamp) are
#     labelled PII here but must lose the label once validators run (T3.4);
#   - seq 107 (valid card) must lose its false Aadhaar match, not its PII label.
# Annotation lines are stream lines too: seq 89 and 91 name the TIMEOUT rule, so they
# match it themselves and are labelled PERF_WARNING (see the header of the corpus).
